    {
      "id": "credimi-collaborative-automation-for-eudi-interoperability-and-conformance-pYLePZ",
      "sector": "public_sector",
      "title": "One EUDI Wallet Release Across OpenID Foundation, WE BUILD and FCAF",
      "summary": "Before releasing a new EUDI Wallet build, a wallet development team must show that the same app can receive and present credentials correctly across independent test ecosystems. Today this often requires separate manual sessions, provider-specific scripts and test code added to the application.\n\nIn the implemented Credimi workflow, a release candidate running on a real Android device is tested against OpenID Foundation and WE BUILD services. The wallet receives a test credential through OpenID4VCI and presents a PID-format SD-JWT VC through OpenID4VP. Credimi automates the wallet actions and API interactions, captures structured results, screenshots, video and device logs, and extracts the applicable FCAF test results from that evidence.\n\nThe developer can identify the failed requirement, fix the wallet and rerun exactly the same journey. Keeping the test logic outside the application substantially reduces implementation effort. The automation pipelines, adapters and evidence definitions can be reused across wallet releases and implementations, turning separate ecosystem tests into a shared and repeatable release-validation process.",
      "organizationName": "Forkbomb",
      "productionDeployment": "yes",
      "status": "published",
